00:27:08.960 --> 00:27:09.200
Yeah.
对。

598
00:27:09.480 --> 00:27:11.180
But I didn't know what Brian did.
但我不知道布兰恩是怎么做的。

599
00:27:11.460 --> 00:27:12.740
So I texted him.
所以我给他发了短信。

600
00:27:12.800 --> 00:27:16.160
And he said he also really transferred the calls.
他说他也是真的转接了电话。

601
00:27:16.540 --> 00:27:21.360
But he would have to remember the extensions because he was running around.
但他必须记住分机号，因为他到处跑。

602
00:27:21.700 --> 00:27:24.880
After the first transfer, he couldn't take his slip of paper with him anymore.
在第一次转接之后，他就再也不能随身带着写着号码的小纸条了。

603
00:27:25.100 --> 00:27:25.460
Right.
对。

604
00:27:25.660 --> 00:27:26.280
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

605
00:27:26.280 --> 00:27:31.680
I still have a photo of all of our transfer numbers that was taped to my phone.
我手机上还存着一张我们所有转接分机号的照片，是用胶带贴在手机上的。

606
00:27:31.980 --> 00:27:33.060
I took a picture of it.
我拍下了它。

607
00:27:33.260 --> 00:27:33.420
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

608
00:27:34.400 --> 00:27:39.720
Well, in the DVD commentary, Matt Sohn, our camera operator, shared with us that on the
嗯，在DVD评论音轨中，我们的摄影师马特·孙跟我们分享说，在

609
00:27:39.720 --> 00:27:44.540
day they were filming, Brian was doing the transferring, but they were having some issues
他们拍摄的那天，布莱恩在负责转接，但电话

610
00:27:44.540 --> 00:27:45.300
with the phones.
出了一些问题。

611
00:27:45.360 --> 00:27:50.240
And so they weren't going to some of the desk clumps they were supposed to.
所以他们没有去那些本该去的办公桌群。

612
00:27:50.500 --> 00:27:54.920
And so Brian actually ended up running around to wherever it was ringing.
因此，布莱恩实际上最终跑向了任何响铃的地方。

613
00:27:55.460 --> 00:27:56.260
Oh, wow.
哦，哇。

614
00:27:56.280 --> 00:27:57.960
So that mania was a little real.
所以那种疯狂是有几分真实的。

615
00:27:58.080 --> 00:27:59.800
He really didn't know where it was going to ring.
他真的不知道电话会在哪里响。

616
00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.000
I think there's at least one time where it didn't ring where it was supposed to.
我觉得至少有一次，电话没有在应响的地方响。

617
00:28:03.100 --> 00:28:03.800
And he just ran.
而他直接就跑了。

618
00:28:04.040 --> 00:28:05.940
And Matt said they were just following him.
马特说他们当时就在后面跟着他。

619
00:28:06.280 --> 00:28:09.540
We had a fan question from Monica in Scranton, Angela.
安吉拉，我们收到了来自斯克兰顿的粉丝莫妮卡的一个问题。

620
00:28:09.720 --> 00:28:10.920
And this one's for you.
这个问题是给你的。

621
00:28:11.120 --> 00:28:11.380
Okay.
好的。

622
00:28:11.680 --> 00:28:18.920
When Angela yells out, you're bad at this too, were you implying that Pam is bad at it
当安吉拉大喊“你这个也不行”时，你是在暗示帕姆不行

623
00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:21.960
and so is Kevin or that Kevin is bad at everything?
凯文也不行，还是说凯文做什么都不行？

624
00:28:22.900 --> 00:28:25.080
Well, first of all, that line is scripted.
嗯，首先，那句台词是写进剧本的。

625
00:28:25.180 --> 00:28:25.960
That was not improv.
那不是即兴发挥。

626
00:28:26.660 --> 00:28:32.460
And I think Angela is just implying that Kevin is horrible at everything.
我觉得安吉拉只是在暗示凯文做什么都很糟糕。

627
00:28:33.260 --> 00:28:36.300
I actually don't think it's a dig at Pam for once.
我其实觉得这次不是在挖苦帕姆。

628
00:28:36.780 --> 00:28:38.740
I think it's more of a dig at Kevin.
我觉得这更像是在挖苦凯文。

629
00:28:38.960 --> 00:28:42.380
We also got a piece of mail from Grace B who said,
我们还收到了一封来自格蕾丝·B的信，她说，

630
00:28:42.380 --> 00:28:45.180
Kevin taught me how to transfer a call.
凯文教我怎么转接电话。

631
00:28:45.380 --> 00:28:48.340
She said she was an office aide in high school.
她说她在高中时当过办公室助理。

632
00:28:48.560 --> 00:28:50.120
They got a new phone system.
他们换了新电话系统。

633
00:28:50.360 --> 00:28:53.400
She wasn't sure what to do, but she remembered this episode,
她不知道该怎么办，但她想起了这一集，

634
00:28:53.720 --> 00:28:56.380
transfer extension transfer, and it worked.
转接、分机、转接，然后成功了。

635
00:28:56.580 --> 00:28:57.680
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

636
00:28:57.720 --> 00:28:58.940
So she says thank you.
所以她说谢谢你们。

637
00:28:59.120 --> 00:28:59.940
You're welcome.
不客气。

638
00:29:00.360 --> 00:29:04.640
Well, in the script, when Kevin finally gets the call to Andy,
嗯，在剧本里，当凯文终于把电话转给安迪时，

639
00:29:04.920 --> 00:29:06.720
this was the stage direction.
舞台说明是这样的。

640
00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:11.280
People ad lib, way to go, all right, applaud, giving Kevin fist bumps.
大家即兴发挥，干得好，太棒了，鼓掌，和凯文碰拳。

641
00:29:11.280 --> 00:29:12.860
He is very happy.
他非常高兴。

642
00:29:13.100 --> 00:29:16.620
In the background of Andy's talking head, the celebration continues.
在安迪的单人访谈背景中，庆祝活动仍在继续。

643
00:29:16.820 --> 00:29:19.580
Kevin shakes up a soda can and opens it.
凯文摇晃着一罐苏打水并将其打开。

644
00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:24.880
That's very Dream Team-esque.
那很有“梦之队”的风范。

645
00:29:25.040 --> 00:29:25.540
I know.
我知道。

646
00:29:25.740 --> 00:29:26.940
Very sports celebration.
非常有体育夺冠庆祝的感觉。

647
00:29:26.940 --> 00:29:27.580
I know.
我知道。

648
00:29:27.940 --> 00:29:32.000
Well, now Pam is going to arrive for her first day of work.
嗯，现在帕姆要来上班了，今天是她上班的第一天。

649
00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:32.620
First day?
第一天？

650
00:29:32.740 --> 00:29:34.200
There's a sign and everything.
有标语牌还有各种东西呢。

651
00:29:34.460 --> 00:29:35.000
I know.
我知道。

652
00:29:35.200 --> 00:29:35.880
It's official.
这是官方决定的。

653
00:29:36.180 --> 00:29:38.260
I don't know if you noticed her little blazer.
我不知道你们有没有注意到她那个小西装外套。

654
00:29:38.400 --> 00:29:39.080
I did.
我注意到了。

655
00:29:39.360 --> 00:29:42.520
There was a very big wardrobe discussion.
为此我们进行了一场非常激烈的服装讨论。

656
00:29:42.520 --> 00:29:44.540
Before we started this arc, yes.
在我们开始这个单元之前，是的。

657
00:29:44.780 --> 00:29:47.240
For what Pam's I'm a paper salesman outfit is?
为了弄清楚潘恩“我是个卖纸的”这套衣服是怎样的？

658
00:29:47.360 --> 00:29:47.700
Yes.
是的。

659
00:29:47.880 --> 00:29:49.060
So here's one thing.
所以这里有个情况。

660
00:29:49.060 --> 00:29:52.540
We originally thought, should she wear a pants suit?
我们最初考虑过，她该穿裤装吗？

661
00:29:52.760 --> 00:29:54.160
Like kind of a power suit.
有点像那种权力套装。

662
00:29:54.300 --> 00:29:55.560
So bold, Pam.
太大胆了，潘恩。

663
00:29:55.800 --> 00:29:56.840
But listen to this.
但听我说这个。

664
00:29:57.040 --> 00:30:04.360
In an earlier season, there had been a discussion about if Pam could sometimes wear pants to the
在更早的一季里，曾讨论过潘恩是否有时可以在办公室穿裤子

665
00:30:04.360 --> 00:30:09.520
office because she had such a uniform of her cardigan and her pencil skirt and everything.
因为她总是穿着开衫和铅笔裙之类的制服。

666
00:30:09.760 --> 00:30:11.900
And it went all the way up to the network.
而且这件事一直汇报到了电视台高层。

667
00:30:12.080 --> 00:30:16.080
And the network said, Pam must wear pencil skirts.
电视台说，潘恩必须穿铅笔裙。

668
00:30:17.100 --> 00:30:17.620
Yeah.
是啊。

669
00:30:17.900 --> 00:30:18.160
Okay.
好吧。

670
00:30:18.260 --> 00:30:20.160
I have wondered about this, Jenna.
我一直很好奇这件事，珍娜。

671
00:30:20.300 --> 00:30:21.540
And I've never told you this.
而且我从来没跟你说过。

672
00:30:21.740 --> 00:30:25.420
But for a few episodes, they put Angela Martin in dress pants.
但在有几集里，他们让安吉拉·马丁穿了正装裤。

673
00:30:25.580 --> 00:30:25.980
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

674
00:30:25.980 --> 00:30:27.760
And then all of a sudden, the pants went away.
然后突然之间，裤子就没了。

675
00:30:27.920 --> 00:30:31.260
And so I went to wardrobe and I said, hey, can we bring back the dress pants?
所以我去找服装组说，嘿，我们能把正装裤穿回来吗？

676
00:30:31.340 --> 00:30:32.080
Those are so comfortable.
那些穿着太舒服了。

677
00:30:32.280 --> 00:30:35.860
And they said, oh, actually, we got a note that they just want you in skirts.
他们说，哦，其实我们接到通知，他们就想让你穿裙子。

678
00:30:36.300 --> 00:30:37.220
Isn't that interesting?
这不有趣吗？

679
00:30:37.560 --> 00:30:39.660
I did not know you got the same note.
我不知道你也收到了同样的通知。

680
00:30:39.760 --> 00:30:40.780
I thought that was crazy.
我觉得这太疯狂了。

681
00:30:41.240 --> 00:30:44.060
And so we were reminded that I could not wear a pantsuit.
所以我们被提醒我不能穿裤装。

682
00:30:44.240 --> 00:30:45.720
We had to keep the pencil skirt.
我们必须保留铅笔裙。

683
00:30:46.060 --> 00:30:49.080
So only thing we could change was the top half of my body.
所以我们唯一能改变的只有我上半身的衣服。

684
00:30:49.080 --> 00:30:54.440
Who was the brass at the top of NBC that was like, office ladies must wear skirts?
NBC高层里到底是哪个领导要求办公室女性必须穿裙子的？

685
00:30:54.680 --> 00:30:57.060
Well, look at Phyllis, always in a skirt.
你看菲利斯，总是穿着裙子。

686
00:30:57.360 --> 00:30:59.120
Meredith, always in some kind of jumper.
梅雷迪思，总是穿着某种套头裙。

687
00:30:59.480 --> 00:30:59.840
Kelly.
凯利。

688
00:31:00.140 --> 00:31:00.420
Kelly.
凯利。

689
00:31:00.940 --> 00:31:01.420
Jan.
简。

690
00:31:02.520 --> 00:31:03.560
And Nellie.
还有内莉。

691
00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:04.840
Skirts.
裙子。

692
00:31:05.060 --> 00:31:07.880
However, Karen always wore pants.
然而，凯伦总是穿裤子。

693
00:31:08.060 --> 00:31:09.380
I don't think she ever wore a skirt.
我觉得她从来没穿过裙子。

694
00:31:09.540 --> 00:31:11.980
And I think that sometimes Holly wore pants.
而且我觉得霍莉有时也会穿裤子。

695
00:31:12.160 --> 00:31:12.820
Am I right?
我没记错吧？

696
00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:16.020
But mostly, it was dresses and skirts.
但大多数情况下，都是连衣裙和半身裙。

697
00:31:16.320 --> 00:31:17.640
Joe Bennett wore pants.
乔·贝内特穿的是裤子。

698
00:31:17.640 --> 00:31:19.440
But those were all guest stars.
但那些全都是客串演员。

699
00:31:19.900 --> 00:31:22.100
Core cast had to be in skirts, I guess.
我猜核心演员必须穿裙子。

700
00:31:22.420 --> 00:31:23.020
I don't know.
我不知道。

701
00:31:23.140 --> 00:31:25.000
Who was the network brass at the time?
当时的高层是谁？

702
00:31:25.140 --> 00:31:26.820
Was it the guy from Mad Men?
是《广告狂人》里的那个家伙吗？

703
00:31:27.000 --> 00:31:28.580
Was Don Draper running the network?
唐·德雷珀在管理电视台吗？

704
00:31:29.720 --> 00:31:30.500
Is that who?
是这个人吗？

705
00:31:31.100 --> 00:31:31.540
Maybe.
也许吧。

706
00:31:31.920 --> 00:31:33.520
I feel a soapbox a coming.
我感觉有人又要长篇大论了。

707
00:31:34.020 --> 00:31:34.980
No, I'm going to leave it.
不，我不说了。

708
00:31:35.040 --> 00:31:35.680
I'll leave it.
我不说了。

709
00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:36.500
Let's leave it.
算了吧，不说了。

710
00:31:36.780 --> 00:31:37.760
Everyone knows it.
大家都知道。

711
00:31:38.040 --> 00:31:38.880
They heard it.
他们都听说了。

712
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:39.600
They heard it.
他们都听说了。

713
00:31:39.680 --> 00:31:40.160
It was subtle.
这很微妙。

714
00:31:40.320 --> 00:31:40.660
It was there.
但它是存在的。

715
00:31:41.320 --> 00:31:41.560
Okay.
好吧。

716
00:31:41.880 --> 00:31:43.960
So bottom line is, here's what we did.
所以总而言之，我们是这么做的。

717
00:31:44.100 --> 00:31:46.820
I switched out my pantyhose for tights.
我把连裤袜换成了紧身裤袜。

718
00:31:47.400 --> 00:31:51.480
I'm wearing a little bit more of a heel, bit of a power shoe, and a blazer.
我穿了稍微高一点的鞋跟，有点像权力鞋，还穿了一件西装外套。

719
00:31:51.740 --> 00:31:54.120
So they were little changes, but they did feel impactful.
所以这些都是小改变，但确实很有冲击力。

720
00:31:54.400 --> 00:31:57.140
I thought Pam felt a little more polished.
我觉得帕姆看起来更干练了些。

721
00:31:58.000 --> 00:31:58.880
That was our goal.
这就是我们的目标。

722
00:31:59.240 --> 00:32:02.480
Well, Michael is going to start his first day of work in a bathrobe.
迈克尔第一天上班竟然穿着浴袍。

723
00:32:02.800 --> 00:32:05.480
Pam's like, Michael, you were expecting me, weren't you?
帕姆就说，迈克尔，你本该料到我会来的，对吧？

724
00:32:05.700 --> 00:32:06.320
He's like, yeah.
他说，是啊。

725
00:32:06.820 --> 00:32:07.140
Yeah.
是啊。

726
00:32:07.200 --> 00:32:09.840
She's like, are you wearing anything under the robe?
她就问，你浴袍里面穿衣服了吗？

727
00:32:09.840 --> 00:32:11.380
And he's like, that's inappropriate.
然后他说，这不太合适。

728
00:32:11.860 --> 00:32:19.380
He brings her inside, and he actually has set up his dining room sort of office-like.
他把她带进屋里，他的餐厅其实已经布置得像个办公室一样了。

729
00:32:19.400 --> 00:32:20.080
It's nice.
挺不错的。

730
00:32:20.420 --> 00:32:21.080
It is nice.
确实不错。

731
00:32:21.080 --> 00:32:24.900
I think these are all items he took from the supply chest as he was leaving.
我觉得这些都是他离开时从储藏室拿的东西。

732
00:32:25.060 --> 00:32:25.360
Clearly.
很明显。

733
00:32:25.360 --> 00:32:27.680
And he starts making French toaSt.
然后他开始做法国吐司。

734
00:32:28.280 --> 00:32:30.060
A lot of French toaSt.
做了好多法国吐司。

735
00:32:30.440 --> 00:32:36.500
And there was a deleted Pam talking head where she explains her motivation to join Michael.
有一个被删掉的帕姆单人采访镜头，她在里面解释了自己加入迈克尔的动机。

736
00:32:36.780 --> 00:32:40.320
She steps outside on the patio while he's making French toaSt.
就在他做法国吐司的时候，她走到露台上。

737
00:32:40.500 --> 00:32:40.980
Here it is.
就是这个。

738
00:32:40.980 --> 00:32:43.100
I felt ready for a change.
我觉得自己准备好迎接改变了。

739
00:32:43.640 --> 00:32:49.740
After all these years at Dunder Mifflin, I just wasn't getting the same rush that I used to get from being a receptioniSt.
在邓德米夫林待了这么多年之后，我做前台已经找不到以前那种刺激感了。

740
00:32:50.500 --> 00:32:51.600
This feels good.
感觉真不错。

741
00:32:52.980 --> 00:32:54.120
This egg won't crack.
这鸡蛋敲不开。

742
00:32:54.520 --> 00:32:54.820
Oh.
哦。

743
00:32:55.260 --> 00:32:55.620
Okay.
好吧。

744
00:32:58.010 --> 00:32:59.290
The egg won't crack.
鸡蛋敲不开。

745
00:32:59.410 --> 00:32:59.770
Yeah.
是啊。

746
00:32:59.950 --> 00:33:02.750
He interrupts her to help him crack eggs.
他打断她是为了让她帮自己敲鸡蛋。

747
00:33:03.110 --> 00:33:05.070
Pam enjoys her French toaSt.
帕姆吃得很享受她的法国吐司。

748
00:33:05.310 --> 00:33:06.370
It was very good.
非常好吃。

749
00:33:06.510 --> 00:33:07.030
I ate it.
我把它吃光了。

750
00:33:07.210 --> 00:33:08.010
Did you really?
真的吗？

751
00:33:08.010 --> 00:33:08.770
It was delicious.
太好吃了。

752
00:33:09.450 --> 00:33:10.930
That was just real.
太真实了。

753
00:33:11.190 --> 00:33:12.330
Way to go, prop food.
真有你的，道具食物。

754
00:33:12.330 --> 00:33:12.950
I know.
我知道。

755
00:33:13.130 --> 00:33:17.610
We had a fan question from Isla H who said, who had to make all the French toast?
我们收到了来自Isla H的粉丝提问，她问，是谁做了所有的法式吐司？

756
00:33:17.910 --> 00:33:19.410
Phil Shea and his team.
菲尔·谢伊和他的团队。

757
00:33:19.650 --> 00:33:21.110
They made a bunch of French toaSt.
他们做了好多法式吐司。

758
00:33:21.270 --> 00:33:22.250
But here's the problem.
但问题来了。

759
00:33:22.530 --> 00:33:24.350
Michael won't stop making French toaSt.
迈克尔一直在做法式吐司停不下来。

760
00:33:24.970 --> 00:33:32.350
And Pam realizes it's because he's having some feelings about really getting started in this new company.
而帕姆意识到这是因为他对在这家新公司真正起步有些情绪。

761
00:33:32.770 --> 00:33:35.390
She tries to get him to stop mixing the eggs.
她试图让他停止搅拌鸡蛋。

762
00:33:35.910 --> 00:33:38.750
And it ends up spilling eggs all over him.
结果鸡蛋洒了他一身。

763
00:33:38.970 --> 00:33:41.430
All over him and into his crocs.
洒满全身，还流进了他的洞洞鞋里。

764
00:33:41.430 --> 00:33:43.050
We got questions about that.
我们收到了关于这方面的提问。

765
00:33:43.190 --> 00:33:45.750
People wanted to know, was it real egg in the bowl?
大家想知道，碗里的真的是鸡蛋吗？

766
00:33:46.150 --> 00:33:49.450
Was the line, I have egg in my crocs improvised?
“我洞洞鞋里有鸡蛋”这句台词是即兴发挥的吗？

767
00:33:49.790 --> 00:33:53.670
And people were also curious, how did we do this scene?
大家还很好奇，我们是怎么拍这场戏的？

768
00:33:53.690 --> 00:33:58.710
Because it seems difficult to have the egg go in the same place each time.
因为每次都要让鸡蛋溅到同一个地方似乎很难。

769
00:33:59.090 --> 00:34:03.310
Well, I will say that Steve did improvise the line, I have egg in my crocs.
嗯，我要说的是，史蒂夫确实即兴说出了“我洞洞鞋里有鸡蛋”这句台词。

770
00:34:04.830 --> 00:34:08.410
It was very hard not to laugh, but it's true.
要忍住不笑真的很难，但这是真的。

771
00:34:08.990 --> 00:34:14.750
We couldn't get the egg to splash in the same way every time, so I could not laugh because this was a one-er.
我们无法让鸡蛋每次都以同样的方式溅出来，所以我不能笑，因为这是一镜到底。

772
00:34:14.910 --> 00:34:16.570
We would have to use a whole take.
我们必须使用一整条完整的镜头。

773
00:34:16.730 --> 00:34:19.430
We couldn't cut between different takes because the egg would be different.
我们不能在不同的镜头之间剪辑，因为鸡蛋的情况会不一样。

774
00:34:19.710 --> 00:34:21.070
Oh, so much pressure.
哦，压力太大了。

775
00:34:21.310 --> 00:34:23.270
It's so hard to not laugh with Steve.
跟史蒂夫对戏时要忍住不笑太难了。

776
00:34:23.490 --> 00:34:23.990
I know.
我懂。

777
00:34:24.210 --> 00:34:25.110
But I didn't.
但我忍住了。

778
00:34:25.170 --> 00:34:29.690
But I think you can tell how hard I am trying not to laugh in the scene.
不过我觉得你能看出我在那场戏里憋笑憋得有多辛苦。

779
00:34:29.810 --> 00:34:30.410
Do you look constipated or something?
你看上去像便秘了还是怎么的？

780
00:34:30.410 --> 00:34:31.150
Yeah, I do.
对，确实像。

781
00:34:31.310 --> 00:34:34.710
I look like, you can tell I'm like tensely holding in.
我看起来，你能看出我在极力忍耐。

782
00:34:34.810 --> 00:34:35.710
It works, though.
不过效果很好。

783
00:34:35.850 --> 00:34:41.970
It just looks like Pam is like watching someone who she thinks is supposed to know what they're doing, who clearly doesn't.
看起来就像是帕姆在看着一个她以为懂行、但实际上根本不懂的人。

784
00:34:42.070 --> 00:34:42.810
She's like, oh, crap.
她心里想，糟了。

785
00:34:42.910 --> 00:34:43.930
What have I gotten myself into?
我到底卷进什么里了？

786
00:34:44.250 --> 00:34:50.390
Well, we did do several takes of this, and it was a big reset every time because we would have to clean up all the eggs in the kitchen.
嗯，我们确实拍了好几条，而且每次都要花好大功夫重置，因为我们得清理厨房里的所有鸡蛋。

787
00:34:50.410 --> 00:34:52.370
We'd have to clean up all the eggs on Steve.
我们得清理史蒂夫身上的所有鸡蛋。

788
00:34:52.370 --> 00:34:54.330
He would have to change his bathrobe.
他得换掉浴袍。

789
00:34:54.850 --> 00:34:56.370
But this one was perfect.
但这条完美。

790
00:34:56.430 --> 00:34:58.810
This was the time he improvised that line.
这就是他即兴说出那句台词的那一次。

791
00:34:58.810 --> 00:35:00.690
And the egg just went everywhere.
而且鸡蛋到处都是。

792
00:35:01.150 --> 00:35:04.690
So I also knew as I was standing there, this is the one.
所以我站在那儿的时候也知道，就是这条了。

793
00:35:05.070 --> 00:35:06.490
Do not mess this up.
千万别搞砸了。

794
00:35:06.670 --> 00:35:06.870
Right.
没错。

795
00:35:07.250 --> 00:35:15.190
So one thing to point out, you guys, which I love about our show, to nerd out on you for a minute, since Steve improvised the line, eggs in my Crocs,
所以有一点我要指出，大家伙儿，我特别喜欢我们剧的一点，跟你们稍微探讨一下专业细节，既然史蒂夫即兴说出了“我洞洞鞋里有鸡蛋”这句台词，

796
00:35:15.330 --> 00:35:19.330
that meant our camera operator had to improvise the move to pan down to his feet.
那就意味着我们的摄像师必须即兴做出下移镜头去拍他脚部的动作。

797
00:35:19.530 --> 00:35:19.850
Yes.
是的。

798
00:35:19.850 --> 00:35:22.530
That wouldn't have been planned, but that sells the joke.
这本来不在计划中，但这就把笑点撑起来了。

799
00:35:22.890 --> 00:35:24.010
So good.
太棒了。

800
00:35:24.170 --> 00:35:25.370
Such a great two-hander.
真是一场精彩的对手戏。

801
00:35:25.630 --> 00:35:29.710
We also had a fan catch in this scene in the kitchen.
我们在这一场厨房戏里也发现了一个粉丝彩蛋。

802
00:35:30.190 --> 00:35:31.070
Sierra G.
塞拉·G.

803
00:35:31.390 --> 00:35:32.310
and Lauren W.
和劳伦·W.

804
00:35:32.630 --> 00:35:39.190
point out that at 4 minutes 31 seconds, there's a sign on his kitchen counter that says, his.
指出在4分31秒时，他厨房台面上有一个牌子写着“他的”。

805
00:35:39.810 --> 00:35:40.210
Yeah.
对。

806
00:35:40.210 --> 00:35:41.690
But there is no hers.
但没有“她的”。

807
00:35:42.150 --> 00:35:42.417
Hers.
“她的”。

808
00:35:42.417 --> 00:35:43.270
I saw that, too.
我也看到了。

809
00:35:43.270 --> 00:35:46.770
And they were like, I guess Jan took the hers when she left.
他们就说，我猜简走的时候把“她的”拿走了。

810
00:35:47.370 --> 00:35:50.130
Or maybe she never even wanted hers out.
或者她根本就没想把“她的”摆出来。

811
00:35:50.850 --> 00:35:52.690
Maybe Michael just bought a his.
也许迈克尔只买了一个“他的”。

812
00:35:52.830 --> 00:35:55.390
I think he bought a his, her, and she never put hers out.
我觉得他买了“他的”和“她的”，但她从没把“她的”摆出来。

813
00:35:55.590 --> 00:35:56.150
I don't know.
我不知道。

814
00:35:56.330 --> 00:35:58.330
It's sad no matter how it shook out.
不管怎么说，这结果都挺让人难过的。

815
00:35:58.550 --> 00:36:01.850
Should we go back to the office and see what's happening back there?
我们要不要回办公室看看那边在发生什么？

816
00:36:02.210 --> 00:36:05.450
Yes, because this was a really fun conference room scene.
好啊，因为这是一个非常有趣的会议室场景。

817
00:36:05.450 --> 00:36:08.410
We were having a absolute blast with Idris.
我们和伊德瑞斯玩得超级开心。

818
00:36:08.890 --> 00:36:15.670
He's holding court the way Michael used to, and he's telling them how things are going to proceed now that they've lost two employees.
他像以前的迈克尔一样掌控全场，在他们失去了两名员工后，他告诉大家接下来事情会怎么推进。

819
00:36:16.330 --> 00:36:19.030
But Kelly and Angela just want to know more about Charles.
但凯莉和安吉拉只想多了解一些关于查尔斯的事。

820
00:36:19.730 --> 00:36:22.810
I love that Kelly's like, where are you staying in Scranton?
我太喜欢凯莉问的那句：你住在斯克兰顿哪里的酒店？

821
00:36:23.010 --> 00:36:24.210
And he's like, a hotel.
然后他说，一家酒店。

822
00:36:24.350 --> 00:36:25.990
And Angela goes, where were you born?
接着安吉拉问，你在哪儿出生的？

823
00:36:26.450 --> 00:36:27.670
Where were you born?
你在哪儿出生的？

824
00:36:27.810 --> 00:36:28.790
It was so fun.
太好玩了。

825
00:36:28.870 --> 00:36:30.130
It was hard not to laugh.
让人很难忍住不笑。

826
00:36:30.130 --> 00:36:37.970
And I want you guys to know, when Andy asked how the operations of the company are going in the background, I caught Brian out of character.
我想让你们知道，当安迪在背景里问公司运营情况时，我抓拍到了布莱恩出戏的瞬间。

827
00:36:38.490 --> 00:36:40.730
He is clearly just Brian in this moment.
这一刻他显然就是布莱恩本人。

828
00:36:40.750 --> 00:36:43.310
If you go to three minutes, two seconds, it's very subtle.
如果你看3分02秒，非常不明显。

829
00:36:43.430 --> 00:36:44.430
But look at his face.
但看他的脸。

830
00:36:44.690 --> 00:36:46.610
That is Brian and not Kevin.
那是布莱恩，而不是凯文。

831
00:36:46.810 --> 00:36:47.990
I'm going to show you a picture, Jenna.
我要给你看张照片，珍娜。

832
00:36:48.770 --> 00:36:51.370
Because we were just having a great time in this scene.
因为我们在这一场里玩得正开心。

833
00:36:52.390 --> 00:36:55.150
And there were all these moments when you didn't know if you were on camera.
有好多这样的时刻，你都不知道自己是不是在镜头里。

834
00:36:55.230 --> 00:36:56.890
And sometimes, look at that face.
有时，看那个表情。

835
00:36:57.810 --> 00:36:58.530
Oh, that's Brian.
哦，那是布莱恩。

836
00:36:58.710 --> 00:36:59.130
I know.
我知道。

837
00:36:59.130 --> 00:37:00.710
Well, that's 100% Brian.
好吧，百分之百是布莱恩。

838
00:37:01.270 --> 00:37:02.810
He's just trying not to laugh.
他只是在努力憋笑。

839
00:37:02.910 --> 00:37:03.770
And he's looking at John.
而且他在看着约翰。

840
00:37:04.630 --> 00:37:10.790
Well, then we're going to see Phyllis, Creed, and Stanley sort of observing Charles in his office.
接下来我们会看到菲利斯、克里德和斯坦利在观察办公室里的查尔斯。

841
00:37:10.990 --> 00:37:11.850
Charles is on the phone.
查尔斯正在打电话。

842
00:37:12.030 --> 00:37:13.530
They're like, does he eat?
他们就像在说，他吃东西吗？

843
00:37:13.710 --> 00:37:15.110
Does he go to the bathroom?
他去洗手间吗？

844
00:37:15.590 --> 00:37:17.390
He's a total mystery to them.
对他们来说，他完全是个谜。

845
00:37:17.750 --> 00:37:19.270
Jenna, there was more to this.
珍娜，这还有更多的内容。

846
00:37:19.410 --> 00:37:24.090
There was a series of talking heads where everyone in the office is sort of commenting on how Charles is a mystery.
有一系列访谈片段，办公室里的每个人都在评论查尔斯是个谜。

847
00:37:24.450 --> 00:37:26.190
It starts with Angela Martin.
从安吉拉·马丁开始。

848
00:37:26.190 --> 00:37:29.330
Get ready for some titillated Angela.
准备好迎接有点被撩到的安吉拉吧。

849
00:37:30.150 --> 00:37:31.470
Charles is a mystery.
查尔斯是个谜。

850
00:37:32.330 --> 00:37:38.290
I wish there was a way I could curl up by the fire with him and flip right to his last page.
我真希望有什么办法能依偎在他身旁的炉火旁，直接翻到他的人生最后一页。

851
00:37:40.880 --> 00:37:41.400
Okay.
好的。

852
00:37:42.120 --> 00:37:43.920
I am in love with that phrase.
我太喜欢这句话了。

853
00:37:43.920 --> 00:37:49.960
Anyways, the next time I seduce my husband, I'm going to say, baby, I want to flip right to your last page.
总之，下次我勾引我老公的时候，我要说，宝贝，我想直接翻到你的最后一页。

854
00:37:50.040 --> 00:37:50.860
I know, right?
对吧，我也觉得？

855
00:37:50.860 --> 00:37:51.660
Let's see what he says.
看他怎么说。

856
00:37:52.020 --> 00:37:53.100
I love that.
我太喜欢了。

857
00:37:53.340 --> 00:37:54.700
I thought that was amazing.
我觉得这太棒了。

858
00:37:54.980 --> 00:37:56.460
And then Toby has one.
然后托比有一个。

859
00:37:56.580 --> 00:38:00.280
And Toby basically is like, I don't know why everyone thinks Charles is a mystery.
托比基本上就说，我不知道为什么大家都觉得查尔斯是个谜。

860
00:38:00.400 --> 00:38:04.040
If anyone would just come back and talk to me, I can share with you.
如果有人能回来跟我聊聊，我就可以跟你们分享。

861
00:38:04.180 --> 00:38:07.440
I have a lot of information about him if anyone just wants to talk to me.
如果有人只想跟我聊聊，我有很多关于他的信息。

862
00:38:07.440 --> 00:38:10.300
I mean, I'm sure Toby does know where he was born, I guess.
我是说，我敢肯定托比确实知道他出生在哪里，我猜。

863
00:38:10.420 --> 00:38:10.660
Yeah.
是啊。

864
00:38:11.080 --> 00:38:14.300
And then Jenna, Charles had a really big talking head.
然后珍娜，查尔斯有一个非常重要的单人访谈镜头。

865
00:38:14.500 --> 00:38:15.800
He's super relaxed.
他超级放松。

866
00:38:15.980 --> 00:38:17.200
This is what it said in the script.
剧本里是这么写的。

867
00:38:17.560 --> 00:38:23.840
Charles seems relaxed, his guard down, speaking casually to the camera in a way he never would to his employees.
查尔斯看起来很放松，放下了戒备，以一种对员工绝不会有的方式对着镜头随意交谈。

868
00:38:24.460 --> 00:38:24.920
Oh.
哦。

869
00:38:25.160 --> 00:38:26.940
And this is what was in the shooting draft.
而这是拍摄剧本里的内容。

870
00:38:27.680 --> 00:38:34.840
Mysterious, just because I show some restraint with my employees when it comes to talking about my personal life, doesn't mean there's some big mystery.
神秘，仅仅因为我在谈论个人生活时对员工有所保留，并不意味着有什么天大的秘密。

871
00:38:35.240 --> 00:38:38.740
I grew up in a suburb of D.C., middle-class family.
我在华盛顿特区的一个郊区长大，中产阶级家庭。

872
00:38:39.020 --> 00:38:46.420
My dad was a CPA, went to University of Maryland, studied business, engaged once, childhood friend, didn't work out.
我爸爸是个注册会计师，就读于马里兰大学，学的是商科，订过一次婚，青梅竹马，没能走到最后。

873
00:38:46.820 --> 00:38:48.640
Then he shows a picture to the camera.
然后他向镜头展示了一张照片。

874
00:38:49.200 --> 00:38:50.420
I'll always love her.
我永远都会爱她。

875
00:38:51.440 --> 00:38:55.020
Then I get my hair cut on the first day of every month, so I remember.
然后我每个月的第一天都会剪头发，这样我就能记住。

876
00:38:55.560 --> 00:38:57.620
There's always less to cut on March 1St.
3月1日总是没多少头发可剪。

877
00:38:58.800 --> 00:39:01.260
I like sour foods, but I hate grapefruit.
我喜欢酸的食物，但我讨厌西柚。

878
00:39:01.480 --> 00:39:02.180
Couldn't tell you why.
说不上为什么。

879
00:39:02.360 --> 00:39:03.040
Just don't get it.
就是不懂。

880
00:39:03.340 --> 00:39:05.000
I have a parakeet named Murphy.
我养了一只叫墨菲的长尾小鹦鹉。

881
00:39:06.540 --> 00:39:08.080
Trying to teach it to talk.
正试图教它说话。

882
00:39:08.220 --> 00:39:11.020
It repeats whatever I say if the thing I say is squawk.
我说了什么它就重复什么，如果我说的话是“呱”。

883
00:39:13.130 --> 00:39:13.510
Person.
人。

884
00:39:13.730 --> 00:39:14.150
I know.
我知道。

885
00:39:14.610 --> 00:39:15.690
Oh, my gosh.
噢，天哪。

886
00:39:16.170 --> 00:39:18.610
Those talking heads would have filled out the rest of the story.
那些单人访谈镜头本可以填满故事的其余部分。

887
00:39:18.890 --> 00:39:21.290
I wonder if that talking head exists somewhere.
我不知道那个单人访谈镜头是不是还在哪个地方存在着。

888
00:39:21.710 --> 00:39:22.390
I don't know.
我不知道。

889
00:39:22.730 --> 00:39:23.130
Dave Rogers.
戴夫·罗杰斯。

890
00:39:23.450 --> 00:39:26.050
Dave Rogers does it because that is priceless.
戴夫·罗杰斯干得出来，因为那太无价了。

891
00:39:26.390 --> 00:39:30.070
But the Angela and Toby one are in the deleted scenes on the DVD.
但安吉拉和托比的片段在DVD的删减片段里。

892
00:39:30.670 --> 00:39:34.710
Back at Michael's condo, he is doing some ab exercises.
回到迈克尔的公寓，他正在做腹肌锻炼。

893
00:39:35.230 --> 00:39:36.310
He is.
他确实在做。

894
00:39:36.630 --> 00:39:41.170
And Jenna, if you have a camera operator on a DVD commentary, here are some things you'd learn.
而且珍娜，如果你在DVD评论音轨里有一个摄像师，以下是你回学到的东西。

895
00:39:41.470 --> 00:39:48.130
While Michael's doing his sit-ups, the shot that's on Pam at 4 minutes 45 seconds, that was Matt Soen.
在迈克尔做仰卧起坐时，4分45秒时拍潘的那个镜头，那是马特·索恩。

896
00:39:48.410 --> 00:39:48.930
Oh.
哦。

897
00:39:49.150 --> 00:39:50.310
You were his shot.
那是你拍的镜头。

898
00:39:50.610 --> 00:39:50.910
Okay.
好吧。

899
00:39:51.630 --> 00:39:52.370
I don't know.
我不知道。

900
00:39:52.450 --> 00:39:53.210
I just love that.
我就是喜欢这个。

901
00:39:53.510 --> 00:39:56.050
We had a fan question from Gianna W.
我们收到了吉安娜·W 的一个粉丝提问。

902
00:39:56.370 --> 00:40:02.370
When Michael is working out in his condo, is that supposed to be the core blaster from the money episode that he's using?
迈克尔在他的公寓里锻炼时，他用的那个东西是《金钱》那一集里出现的核心训练器吗？

903
00:40:03.150 --> 00:40:05.190
Remember he spent his money on a core blaster?
还记得他把钱花在核心训练器上了吗？

904
00:40:05.730 --> 00:40:06.810
I think so.
我想是的。

905
00:40:07.110 --> 00:40:08.490
I went to the script.
我翻看了剧本。

906
00:40:08.710 --> 00:40:13.870
It doesn't say specifically, but I was so charmed by the scene description in the script.
