But I liked a good guy like Jim deciding to do it.
但我喜欢像吉姆这样的好人决定这么做。

1060
00:46:29.010 --> 00:46:29.230
Hmm.
嗯。

1061
00:46:30.390 --> 00:46:30.830
Interesting.
有意思。

1062
00:46:31.070 --> 00:46:31.370
Right?
对吧？

1063
00:46:31.670 --> 00:46:35.970
I just love that BJ takes moments like that and then puts it into his episodes.
我太喜欢BJ捕捉这样的时刻并把它写进剧集里的做法了。

1064
00:46:36.230 --> 00:46:36.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1065
00:46:36.770 --> 00:46:39.570
No, he reflects on things in the moment and they stay with him.
不，他会当场反思事情，并把这些感悟留在心里。

1066
00:46:39.630 --> 00:46:41.450
He's a very thoughtful person in that way.
从这方面来说，他是一个非常善于思考的人。

1067
00:46:42.130 --> 00:46:48.710
Well, Jim is going to suck up by pretending like he played soccer or is a soccer player.
好吧，吉姆要通过假装自己踢过足球或是个足球运动员来拍马屁了。

1068
00:46:48.990 --> 00:46:49.470
I know.
我懂。

1069
00:46:49.610 --> 00:46:51.770
There's this moment where he's like, I'm not going to do it.
有这样一个时刻，他心想，我绝不这么做。

1070
00:46:51.870 --> 00:46:52.510
I'm not going to do it.
我绝不这么做。

1071
00:46:52.590 --> 00:46:56.130
And then he just succumbs and was like, yeah, I'm a player.
然后他还是屈服了，心想，好吧，我是个球员。

1072
00:46:56.510 --> 00:47:00.530
And Dwight could not be happier.
而德怀特开心极了。

1073
00:47:00.770 --> 00:47:02.510
He's like, oh, really, Jim?
他就像是，哦，真的吗，吉姆？

1074
00:47:02.770 --> 00:47:07.050
I have never heard you talk about soccer.
我从来没听你聊过足球。

1075
00:47:07.050 --> 00:47:10.970
And he's like, you should play Charles, the two of you, today.
然后他说，你们俩今天应该和查尔斯一起踢一场。

1076
00:47:11.590 --> 00:47:13.230
And Charles is all about it.
而查尔斯对此求之不得。

1077
00:47:13.330 --> 00:47:15.130
He's like, yes, I would love it.
他就像是，太好了，我非常愿意。

1078
00:47:15.310 --> 00:47:20.630
And Charles's whole demeanor changes toward Jim, toward everyone in the office.
然后查尔斯对吉姆、对办公室里的每个人的态度全变了。

1079
00:47:20.630 --> 00:47:25.430
He's this very sort of smiley guy all of a sudden.
他突然变成了一个非常爱笑的家伙。

1080
00:47:25.650 --> 00:47:25.970
Yeah.
对。

1081
00:47:26.570 --> 00:47:27.670
It's a big difference.
这反差太大了。

1082
00:47:28.090 --> 00:47:29.890
Well, now Jim's going to be in a big pickle.
好吧，现在吉姆要陷入大麻烦了。

1083
00:47:30.090 --> 00:47:33.350
He said he played soccer from second to fourth grade.
他说他从二年级到四年级一直踢足球。

1084
00:47:33.350 --> 00:47:35.030
He was on the orange team.
他在橙队。

1085
00:47:35.230 --> 00:47:36.230
I love that talking head.
我太喜欢那个面对镜头的独白了。

1086
00:47:36.310 --> 00:47:36.810
I do, too.
我也是。

1087
00:47:36.990 --> 00:47:38.110
It made me laugh.
把我逗笑了。

1088
00:47:38.430 --> 00:47:46.470
Well, listen, I think we should take a break because in the second half of the episode, we are going to see this dream team get assembled.
好了，听着，我觉得我们该休息一下了，因为在这一集的后半部分，我们将看到这个梦之队集结。

1089
00:47:46.490 --> 00:47:49.890
And we're going to see Jim have to deal with his soccer promise.
我们还将看到吉姆不得不去兑现他吹过的踢球牛皮。

1090
00:47:50.130 --> 00:47:50.810
It's good stuff.
这绝对是精彩好戏。

1091
00:47:51.050 --> 00:47:51.550
All right.
好了。

1092
00:48:01.480 --> 00:48:02.420
We are back.
我们回来了。

1093
00:48:02.420 --> 00:48:05.180
And you guys, the dream team got Vikram.
各位，梦之队把维克拉姆弄到手了。

1094
00:48:05.360 --> 00:48:06.040
We got him.
我们把他招募了。

1095
00:48:06.540 --> 00:48:10.160
Vikram, played by the awesome Ranjit Chowdhury.
维克拉姆由杰出的兰吉特·乔杜里饰演。

1096
00:48:10.340 --> 00:48:11.840
He was so fun to work with.
和他合作非常开心。

1097
00:48:11.840 --> 00:48:13.500
You know, he passed away last year.
你知道的，他去年去世了。

1098
00:48:13.640 --> 00:48:14.000
I know.
我知道。

1099
00:48:14.260 --> 00:48:15.300
He was so funny.
他太有趣了。

1100
00:48:15.680 --> 00:48:16.880
We're in the car.
我们在车里。

1101
00:48:17.240 --> 00:48:19.000
And, you know, Michael's all excited.
而且，你知道，迈克尔整个人兴奋极了。

1102
00:48:19.520 --> 00:48:21.160
They pull up to the bowling alley.
他们把车开到了保龄球馆外。

1103
00:48:21.320 --> 00:48:22.920
Michael's like, I have to use the bathroom.
迈克尔就说，我得去个洗手间。

1104
00:48:23.520 --> 00:48:25.280
And Vikram has this line.
然后维克拉姆有这么一句台词。

1105
00:48:25.600 --> 00:48:27.760
It's so good, where he says,
太棒了，他是这么说的，

1106
00:48:28.620 --> 00:48:32.040
confidence, it's the food of the wise man, but the liquor of the fool.
自信，是智者的精神食粮，却是愚者的烈酒。

1107
00:48:32.600 --> 00:48:35.440
I was so struck by this when I watched this episode.
我看这集的时候，真的被这句话震撼到了。

1108
00:48:35.600 --> 00:48:36.000
Me, too.
我也是。

1109
00:48:36.000 --> 00:48:44.560
So I Googled it because I thought, is that like an old, I don't know, expression, proverb, like a Greek philosopher?
所以我去谷歌了一下，因为我在想，这难道是什么古老的，我不知道，俗语、谚语，比如希腊哲学家说的？

1110
00:48:45.260 --> 00:48:45.680
No.
并不是。

1111
00:48:45.920 --> 00:48:46.800
It's nowhere.
哪里都查不到。

1112
00:48:47.120 --> 00:48:51.860
There are Reddit threads dedicated to trying to figure out where this line came from.
有专门的红迪网帖子在试图搞清楚这句台词是哪来的。

1113
00:48:51.980 --> 00:48:54.920
There was an article written about this one line.
甚至还有人为这单单一句话写过一篇文章。

1114
00:48:54.940 --> 00:48:55.520
You're kidding.
你在开玩笑吧。

1115
00:48:55.520 --> 00:49:00.460
And how wise it is and how the writer of the article couldn't find its origin either.
文章写得它有多充满智慧，而且文章的作者也找不到它的出处。

1116
00:49:01.580 --> 00:49:04.500
Someone on our writing staff wrote that line.
我们编剧团队里的某个人写了那句台词。

1117
00:49:04.680 --> 00:49:05.780
And we don't know who?
而我们不知道是谁？

1118
00:49:06.340 --> 00:49:07.200
I asked BJ.
我问了BJ。

1119
00:49:07.480 --> 00:49:08.460
I asked Mindy.
我问了明蒂。

1120
00:49:08.640 --> 00:49:09.720
I asked Aaron Schur.
我问了亚伦·舒尔。

1121
00:49:10.020 --> 00:49:11.900
No one can take credit for it.
没有人承认那是自己写的。

1122
00:49:12.240 --> 00:49:14.460
Aaron Schur said something that I really liked.
亚伦·舒尔说了一句我很喜欢的话。

1123
00:49:14.660 --> 00:49:16.440
He said, I don't know.
他说，我不知道。

1124
00:49:16.620 --> 00:49:19.120
Let's give credit to the whole writing staff.
就把功劳记在全体编剧头上吧。

1125
00:49:19.380 --> 00:49:22.580
Like some sort of collective genius came up with this line.
就像某种集体智慧想出了这句台词一样。

1126
00:49:22.740 --> 00:49:26.040
But someone wrote that from the office.
但办公室里确实有人写下了它。

1127
00:49:26.520 --> 00:49:26.780
Brilliant.
太绝了。

1128
00:49:26.780 --> 00:49:28.360
And it's so good.
而且真的太好了。

1129
00:49:28.620 --> 00:49:32.720
And then last week we talked about Vikram having this amazing talking head.
然后上周我们聊到维克拉姆有一个超棒的单人访谈镜头。

1130
00:49:32.820 --> 00:49:33.500
That got deleted.
被剪掉了。

1131
00:49:33.620 --> 00:49:34.260
That got deleted.
被剪掉了。

1132
00:49:34.260 --> 00:49:36.060
This is where it would have lived, you guys.
大家伙，本来这个镜头应该放在这里的。

1133
00:49:36.420 --> 00:49:42.180
Right after the scene in the car where he says this amazing proverb, he would have said,
就在车里那个他说了那句精彩谚语的场景之后，他本该说，

1134
00:49:42.320 --> 00:49:46.000
when you put your telemarketing career on the line, you're not putting much on the line.
当你把电话营销的事业押上时，其实你也没押上什么。

1135
00:49:46.660 --> 00:49:48.900
And Ranjit was just perfection.
而且兰吉特表现得简直完美。

1136
00:49:49.260 --> 00:49:49.760
Everything.
方方面面。

1137
00:49:50.060 --> 00:49:51.160
His delivery.
他的台词演绎。

1138
00:49:51.400 --> 00:49:53.280
I just, I couldn't get enough of him.
我就是，我看不够他。

1139
00:49:53.380 --> 00:49:54.980
Well, you just so believe him.
对啊，你就是对他的表演深信不疑。

1140
00:49:55.180 --> 00:49:55.320
Yeah.
对。

1141
00:49:55.320 --> 00:49:57.700
And our guest actors were always that way.
我们的客串演员一直都这样。

1142
00:49:57.820 --> 00:50:03.660
Allison Jones had this amazing ability to find people who didn't seem like they were acting at all.
艾莉森·琼斯有一种神奇的能力，能找到那些看起来根本不像是在演戏的人。

1143
00:50:03.660 --> 00:50:04.180
Yeah.
对啊。

1144
00:50:04.580 --> 00:50:07.460
Well, Michael is going to go into the bowling alley.
好吧，迈克尔要走进保龄球馆了。

1145
00:50:07.600 --> 00:50:09.200
He wants a pair of nine shoes.
他想要一双九号的鞋。

1146
00:50:09.640 --> 00:50:11.600
Guess who's working the counter?
你猜谁在柜台工作？

1147
00:50:12.180 --> 00:50:12.640
Ryan.
瑞恩。

1148
00:50:13.180 --> 00:50:15.040
Ryan, who's not on the liSt.
瑞恩，根本不在名单上的人。

1149
00:50:17.960 --> 00:50:22.420
You know, Vikram has this great line in the car where he's like, he's been gone a long time.
你知道的，维克拉姆在车里有一句很棒的台词，他说，他去的时间太久了。

1150
00:50:22.420 --> 00:50:24.040
Is it possible he went bowling?
有没有可能他去打保龄球了？

1151
00:50:24.300 --> 00:50:25.860
You know him better than I do.
你比我更了解他。

1152
00:50:25.860 --> 00:50:30.980
And I thought, Jenna, your delivery as Pam was so great when you're like, yeah.
然后我想，珍娜，你演帕姆时表现得太棒了，就像那种，对吧。

1153
00:50:31.520 --> 00:50:32.080
Yeah.
对。

1154
00:50:32.440 --> 00:50:38.660
So Pam goes in and sees what's happening and says, this was not on the list, Michael.
所以帕姆进去看到发生了什么，然后说，这不在清单上，迈克尔。

1155
00:50:38.900 --> 00:50:43.500
And then she looks at the list and then she's like, when did you put this on the list?
接着她看着清单，然后就像是，你是什么时候把这个加到清单上的？

1156
00:50:43.940 --> 00:50:45.120
I loved that.
我太喜欢那个了。

1157
00:50:45.720 --> 00:50:50.120
We notice right away that Ryan is very tan and very blonde.
我们马上注意到瑞安晒得很黑，头发也很金。

1158
00:50:50.620 --> 00:50:51.820
I was really curious.
我真的很好奇。

1159
00:50:51.980 --> 00:50:54.400
When did BJ know he was going to have to do this with his hair?
BJ是什么时候知道他得这样弄头发的？

1160
00:50:54.940 --> 00:50:56.800
This is what he said on the DVD commentary.
这是他在DVD评论音轨里说的。

1161
00:50:57.580 --> 00:51:02.580
So when I was in Germany and wasn't able to be on the show for a while, my character ran off to Thailand.
所以当我在德国、有一段时间无法参演时，我的角色跑去了泰国。

1162
00:51:02.840 --> 00:51:06.600
All I knew about Ryan coming back was that he was going to be blonde.
关于瑞安回归，我所知道的全部就是他会染成金发。

1163
00:51:06.960 --> 00:51:07.680
Now the tan.
还有美黑。

1164
00:51:07.920 --> 00:51:08.940
The tan is great, too.
美黑也很棒。

1165
00:51:09.040 --> 00:51:09.940
The tan is very funny.
美黑非常搞笑。

1166
00:51:10.640 --> 00:51:13.360
I heard of the hair as frosted tips.
我听说这头发是挑染发梢。

1167
00:51:13.520 --> 00:51:16.880
And then when we did it, Mindy, whose idea it was, came in and was like, no, no, no.
然后当我们做的时候，提出这个想法的明蒂走进来，就说，不，不，不。

1168
00:51:17.140 --> 00:51:18.540
We're only going to go for this joke once.
这个笑话我们只能玩一次。

1169
00:51:18.540 --> 00:51:19.620
You have to be completely blonde.
你必须完全染成金发。

1170
00:51:19.960 --> 00:51:24.920
And so we dyed it and I wore a hat in public for weeks trying to save the surprise and save my dignity.
所以我们把它染了，我在公众场合戴了好几周的帽子，试图保持神秘感并保全我的尊严。

1171
00:51:27.080 --> 00:51:32.200
And he goes on to say that he was also touring stand-up during this time.
接着他继续说，在这期间他还在进行单口喜剧巡演。

1172
00:51:32.820 --> 00:51:37.940
So he got a spray-in brown coloring, you know, that you could like dye.
所以他弄了一种喷雾棕色着色剂，你知道的，你可以染的那种。

1173
00:51:37.940 --> 00:51:45.560
And so he sprayed his hair brown and then he went on stage and it started coming off, like dripping off.
然后他把头发喷成棕色，接着他上台了，然后它开始脱落，就像往下滴一样。

1174
00:51:45.760 --> 00:51:47.680
Like what happened to Rudy Giuliani.
就像鲁迪·朱利安尼遭遇的那样。

1175
00:51:48.180 --> 00:51:49.120
Oh, my God.
噢，天哪。

1176
00:51:49.640 --> 00:51:50.600
Same thing.
一模一样。

1177
00:51:51.060 --> 00:51:52.580
Yes, exactly.
对，完全如此。

1178
00:51:52.920 --> 00:51:55.720
So he had to wear this hat, but it was like really stressful.
所以他不得不戴着这顶帽子，但这真的压力很大。

1179
00:51:55.720 --> 00:51:57.160
He was trying to keep it a secret.
他一直在试图保密。

1180
00:51:57.660 --> 00:52:01.980
I've used that spray for when my roots are coming in.
我用过那种喷雾来遮盖长出来的发根。

1181
00:52:02.480 --> 00:52:03.560
It's genius.
这太天才了。

1182
00:52:03.560 --> 00:52:05.500
I love the spray, by the way.
顺便说一句，我很喜欢这种喷雾。

1183
00:52:05.680 --> 00:52:05.980
Yeah.
对。

1184
00:52:06.080 --> 00:52:06.640
It's great.
这很棒。

1185
00:52:06.640 --> 00:52:11.120
But if you get really warm, it will sweat off.
但如果你真的很热，它就会随着汗水流下来。

1186
00:52:11.480 --> 00:52:11.740
Yeah.
对。

1187
00:52:12.340 --> 00:52:12.800
Beware.
小心点。

1188
00:52:14.220 --> 00:52:15.300
Where are we?
我们到哪了？

1189
00:52:15.520 --> 00:52:18.360
I'll give you a little location breakdown on the bowling alley.
我来给大家简单介绍一下保龄球馆的取景地。

1190
00:52:19.000 --> 00:52:23.740
Idle Hour Lanes, which is the sign-out sign, is a real bowling alley in Scranton.
闲时保龄球馆，也就是外景招牌那个，是斯克兰顿的一家真正的保龄球馆。

1191
00:52:23.840 --> 00:52:25.540
We matched their logo.
我们模仿了他们的标志。

1192
00:52:26.160 --> 00:52:28.500
And in Scranton, there's two.
在斯克兰顿，有两家。

1193
00:52:28.740 --> 00:52:31.440
And one of them is next to Poor Richard's.
其中一家就在可怜理查德酒吧旁边。

1194
00:52:31.820 --> 00:52:33.600
Yes, I've been to that one.
是的，我去过那家。

1195
00:52:33.600 --> 00:52:34.520
I thought you had.
我想你肯定去过。

1196
00:52:34.520 --> 00:52:36.220
It's part of the bar, kind of.
它有点像是酒吧的一部分。

1197
00:52:36.300 --> 00:52:39.680
Like when you go into Poor Richard's, you think, at least I thought I was walking into
就像你走进可怜理查德酒吧时，你以为，至少我是以为我走进了

1198
00:52:39.680 --> 00:52:43.240
a bar, but I actually was walking into a bowling alley and then the bar was to the right.
一家酒吧，但实际上我走进了一家保龄球馆，然后酒吧在右边。

1199
00:52:43.880 --> 00:52:44.640
It's interesting.
这很有趣。

1200
00:52:45.180 --> 00:52:51.200
I thought that we were at Pickwick Bowl, which does have a bar next to it, sort of similar
我以为我们在皮克威克保龄球馆，它旁边确实有个酒吧，有点类似

1201
00:52:51.200 --> 00:52:52.760
to the real Idle Hour Lanes.
来到真正的闲时保龄球馆。

1202
00:52:52.760 --> 00:52:57.660
But no, Randy Cordray said that we shot Ours in Canoga Park.
但不是，兰迪·科德雷说我们是在卡诺加公园拍摄的。

1203
00:52:57.860 --> 00:52:59.640
It was a bowling alley in Canoga Park.
那是卡诺加公园的一家保龄球馆。

1204
00:52:59.880 --> 00:53:05.820
I also have a little guest star shout-out to the bowling alley manager who calls Ryan a
我还想特别鸣谢一下保龄球馆经理的客串演员，他管瑞安叫

1205
00:53:05.820 --> 00:53:06.420
shoe bitch.
鞋子婊子。

1206
00:53:07.340 --> 00:53:09.440
He was played by Jim Woods.
这个角色由吉姆·伍兹饰演。

1207
00:53:09.520 --> 00:53:15.020
He has appeared on How I Met Your Mother, Reno 911, and was a regular on the comedy satire
他曾出演过《老爸老妈浪漫史》、《雷诺911》，还是喜剧讽刺剧

1208
00:53:15.020 --> 00:53:17.400
safety geek's, S-V-I.
安全极客 S-V-I 的常驻演员。

1209
00:53:18.080 --> 00:53:22.000
Again, another person who did not seem like an actor to me.
又是一个在我看来不太像演员的人。

1210
