我是说，看现场篮球，特别是如果你能坐到靠近球场的位置，

1523
01:06:05.790 --> 01:06:08.510
it's like an amazing game live.
那种现场比赛简直太棒了。

1524
01:06:08.810 --> 01:06:10.750
I just love the whole hockey community.
我只是喜欢整个冰球圈子的氛围。

1525
01:06:11.150 --> 01:06:12.210
I love everything about it.
我喜欢关于它的一切。

1526
01:06:12.410 --> 01:06:16.330
I went one time and met some of your hockey mom friends.
我有一次去过，还遇到了你的一些冰球妈妈朋友。

1527
01:06:16.470 --> 01:06:16.670
Yeah.
对啊。

1528
01:06:16.890 --> 01:06:21.490
And what I didn't know you guys is that hockey games, they serve beer at 10 in the morning.
姐妹们，我之前不知道的是，冰球比赛早上十点就卖啤酒了。

1529
01:06:21.630 --> 01:06:22.010
They do.
确实如此。

1530
01:06:22.430 --> 01:06:23.710
I was like, oh my gosh.
当时我都惊呆了。

1531
01:06:23.730 --> 01:06:24.350
They sure do.
他们当然卖。

1532
01:06:24.630 --> 01:06:26.630
We have like juice boxes at soccer.
我们在踢足球时只有果汁盒。

1533
01:06:26.630 --> 01:06:27.830
They have beer.
他们有啤酒。

1534
01:06:28.230 --> 01:06:34.390
I remember going to one of our early hockey games for my son, and it was at 7.30 in the
我记得有一次去参加我儿子的早期冰球比赛之一，当时是早上

1535
01:06:34.390 --> 01:06:35.990
morning, and I brought a coffee.
七点半，我带了一杯咖啡。

1536
01:06:36.330 --> 01:06:41.530
And people were like, does anyone want a beer from the concessions?
然后有人问，有人想要小卖部的啤酒吗？

1537
01:06:41.730 --> 01:06:45.190
And I was like, I don't think so, but thank you.
我说，我想不用了，但谢谢你们。

1538
01:06:45.990 --> 01:06:46.890
Pretty amazing.
相当厉害。

1539
01:06:47.630 --> 01:06:48.470
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

1540
01:06:48.930 --> 01:06:53.210
The Dream Team has lost a member, and they get back to Michael's condo.
梦之队少了一名成员，他们回到了迈克尔的公寓。

1541
01:06:53.210 --> 01:06:54.850
So Ryan's going to run inside.
所以瑞安打算跑进去。

1542
01:06:54.990 --> 01:06:57.230
He wants to watch The Closer on TNT.
他想看TNT电视台的《罪案终结》。

1543
01:06:57.230 --> 01:06:57.370
On TNT.
在TNT电视台。

1544
01:06:57.470 --> 01:06:58.670
Very important to him.
这对很重要。

1545
01:06:59.010 --> 01:07:00.790
Pam's upset she can't get out of the car.
帕姆因为下不了车而很不高兴。

1546
01:07:00.970 --> 01:07:02.290
Now Pam's going to spiral.
现在帕姆情绪开始失控了。

1547
01:07:02.730 --> 01:07:03.630
So guess what?
所以你猜怎么着？

1548
01:07:03.830 --> 01:07:04.070
Hmm.
嗯。

1549
01:07:04.530 --> 01:07:06.910
It was not in the script that you stayed in the car.
你留在车里并不是剧本里写的。

1550
01:07:07.110 --> 01:07:07.810
I remember.
我记得。

1551
01:07:08.130 --> 01:07:09.910
It was Jen Salata's idea.
那是珍·萨拉塔的主意。

1552
01:07:10.330 --> 01:07:14.350
And she fought for it to have Pam stay in the car during the scene.
她极力争取让帕姆在这一场戏里留在车里。

1553
01:07:14.350 --> 01:07:19.910
Yeah, I was supposed to get out of the car, and then sort of the idea was lean against
对，本来我得下车，当时的构思是靠在

1554
01:07:19.910 --> 01:07:20.210
it.
车上。

1555
01:07:20.370 --> 01:07:24.570
And part of that was because it would be really easy to stage it camera-wise.
部分原因是从镜头调度上来说这样会非常简单。

1556
01:07:24.790 --> 01:07:24.930
Yeah.
对。

1557
01:07:25.070 --> 01:07:30.810
Well, I loved her staying in the car, and I love this shot at 16 minutes, 22 seconds, when
嗯，我特别喜欢她留在车里，而且我很喜欢16分22秒时的这个镜头，

1558
01:07:30.810 --> 01:07:35.590
you see Pam in the side mirror and Michael standing next to the car.
你能看到后视镜里的帕姆和站在车旁的迈克尔。

1559
01:07:35.750 --> 01:07:36.930
It's such a cool shot.
这镜头太酷了。

1560
01:07:37.170 --> 01:07:39.370
I had to bring a lot of emotion to the scene.
我得为这场戏投入很多情感。

1561
01:07:39.370 --> 01:07:45.190
You had to see Pam be convinced by Michael, and this is one of those moments when Michael
你必须看到帕姆被迈克尔说服，这就是迈克尔

1562
01:07:45.190 --> 01:07:49.470
becomes really good at being a boss.
真正展现出优秀领导才能的时刻之一。

1563
01:07:49.650 --> 01:07:50.670
And he's so serious.
而且他是那么严肃。

1564
01:07:50.670 --> 01:07:51.810
He's like, listen, kiddo.
他就像是在说，听着，小丫头。

1565
01:07:51.950 --> 01:07:52.290
Yeah.
对。

1566
01:07:52.590 --> 01:07:53.170
You quit.
你辞职吧。

1567
01:07:53.450 --> 01:07:54.310
I quit.
我辞职。

1568
01:07:54.610 --> 01:07:54.990
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1569
01:07:55.390 --> 01:07:57.330
So that's the truth.
所以事实就是这样。

1570
01:07:57.570 --> 01:08:04.230
It was very easy to get emotional because to have Steve Carell say, listen, kiddo, I mean,
要酝酿出情绪非常容易，因为听到史蒂夫·卡瑞尔说，听着，小丫头，我是说，

1571
01:08:04.230 --> 01:08:11.250
I know he wasn't much older than us, but he did always have sort of like a wise, fatherly-
我知道他其实没比我们大多少，但他确实一直给人一种充满智慧、像父亲一样的——

1572
01:08:11.250 --> 01:08:11.450
He was our mentor.
他是我们的导师。

1573
01:08:11.610 --> 01:08:11.890
Yeah.
对。

1574
01:08:12.270 --> 01:08:12.930
Like, exactly.
就，完全是这样。

1575
01:08:13.230 --> 01:08:18.830
And so to have your mentor coach you, it felt real, you know?
所以当你的导师指导你时，那种感觉很真实，你知道吗？

1576
01:08:19.030 --> 01:08:20.190
And it made me emotional.
这让我很动情。

1577
01:08:20.610 --> 01:08:25.730
And we just really connected there in a real way, and it was really sweet.
我们在那里真正地产生了共鸣，感觉非常温馨。

1578
01:08:25.890 --> 01:08:29.870
I just love those Pam Michael moments that reminds me of when he came to her art show,
我就是喜欢那些帕姆和迈克尔的温情时刻，这让我想起他去看她画展的时候，

1579
01:08:30.150 --> 01:08:32.070
and he shows up for her.
他为她撑场面。

1580
01:08:32.230 --> 01:08:32.490
Yeah.
对。

1581
01:08:32.490 --> 01:08:33.630
And it was great.
那感觉真棒。

1582
01:08:33.970 --> 01:08:39.450
Well, next we're going to see Michael on the phone, and he's asking Billy Merchant if
接下来我们要看到迈克尔在打电话，他问比利·麦钱特

1583
01:08:39.450 --> 01:08:44.210
he has any free office space anywhere, because they can't work out of Michael's condo anymore.
哪里还有空闲的办公室，因为他们不能再在迈克尔的公寓办公了。

1584
01:08:44.370 --> 01:08:45.550
They're going to throw him out.
他们要把他赶出去了。

1585
01:08:45.630 --> 01:08:49.090
They got a letter, and Billy says, I got something for you.
他们收到了一封信，比利说，我这儿有个好地方。

1586
01:08:49.350 --> 01:08:53.590
It's like a supply room, maybe, but there's also like a shower?
大概像是个杂物间，不过里面好像还有个淋浴间？

1587
01:08:53.910 --> 01:08:57.410
It's also back at the Dunder Mifflin Scranton building.
它其实还在邓德米夫林斯克兰分公司的楼里。

1588
01:08:57.610 --> 01:08:57.770
Yeah.
对。

1589
01:08:58.050 --> 01:08:59.430
I probably should have led with that.
我本来应该先说这个的。

1590
01:09:00.530 --> 01:09:02.390
And that's exactly right.
事实确实如此。

1591
01:09:02.390 --> 01:09:08.270
It's like a supply room closet, but the gang is like, I could work here.
那就像是个杂物间储藏室，但大家却觉得，我可以在这里办公。

1592
01:09:08.630 --> 01:09:08.870
Yeah.
对。

1593
01:09:09.070 --> 01:09:09.930
They can see it.
他们能看到那种可能。

1594
01:09:10.190 --> 01:09:16.410
And it's really sweet, because the episode ends with Michael adding Michael Scott Paper
这真的很温馨，因为剧集以迈克尔把“迈克尔·斯科特纸业公司”

1595
01:09:16.410 --> 01:09:20.910
Company to the little board in the lobby, and Pam's handing him the little letters.
的名字贴到大厅的小告示板上结束，帕姆正把那些小字母递给他。

1596
01:09:20.910 --> 01:09:26.730
Matt Sohn shared that there was a take where instead of you guys already having the letters,
马特·索恩分享说，曾拍过这样一个版本：你们不是已经准备好了字母，

1597
01:09:26.930 --> 01:09:30.030
that you were taking the letters from other people's businesses' names.
而是从别人公司的招牌上抠下字母来用。

1598
01:09:30.070 --> 01:09:30.470
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1599
01:09:30.470 --> 01:09:31.490
I remember that.
我记得那个。

1600
01:09:32.170 --> 01:09:33.330
I remember that.
我记得。

1601
01:09:33.330 --> 01:09:34.870
Which is really funny to me.
这对我来说真的很好笑。

1602
01:09:35.170 --> 01:09:38.070
And there was a tag that didn't make it in the episode.
还有一个标签没能在这一集中播出。

1603
01:09:38.490 --> 01:09:40.030
Kevin is back at reception.
凯文回到了前台。

1604
01:09:40.330 --> 01:09:41.410
The phone rings.
电话铃响了。

1605
01:09:41.770 --> 01:09:43.310
Kevin answers it.
凯文接起电话。

1606
01:09:43.590 --> 01:09:47.290
And he's able to transfer the call to Dwight successfully.
而且他成功地把电话转接给了德怀特。

1607
01:09:47.650 --> 01:09:48.830
He's so happy.
他太高兴了。

1608
01:09:48.990 --> 01:09:50.350
He looks all cocky to camera.
他对镜头露出了十分自得的神情。

1609
01:09:51.050 --> 01:09:54.710
Charles comes out and says, hey, Kevin, I need you to set up a conference call with David
查尔斯出来说，嘿，凯文，我需要你在10分钟内安排一次与大卫

1610
01:09:54.710 --> 01:09:57.070
Wallace and the other branch managers in 10 minutes.
华莱士以及其他分公司经理的电话会议。

1611
01:09:57.070 --> 01:09:58.710
I'll take it in the conference room.
我会在会议室接听。

1612
01:09:59.230 --> 01:10:01.310
Kevin looks like he's going to crap his pants.
凯文看起来吓得快尿裤子了。

1613
01:10:02.070 --> 01:10:03.670
He goes, you got it, boss.
他说，没问题，老板。

1614
01:10:03.850 --> 01:10:08.010
And then he runs out of the office and never comes back.
然后他跑出了办公室，再也没有回来。

1615
01:10:09.330 --> 01:10:14.970
You know, I asked Brian, what was it like to be at the reception desk for that week?
你知道的，我问布莱恩，在那周坐在前台是什么感觉？

1616
01:10:15.190 --> 01:10:18.490
You know, because I noticed throughout the whole episode, he's in the background.
你知道的，因为我发现在整集节目中，他都在背景里。

1617
01:10:18.810 --> 01:10:22.750
And he was doing what I had to do, which is be in the background a lot.
他做着我必须做的事，那就是经常当背景板。

1618
01:10:23.110 --> 01:10:26.970
And he did point out that just because you guys were in the
他也指出，就因为你们在那个

1619
01:10:26.970 --> 01:10:30.950
corner, which is something you've talked about, you know, they would make you guys
角落里，正如你们以前谈过的，他们会让你盘

1620
01:10:30.950 --> 01:10:33.430
stand at the copier.
腿站在复印机旁。

1621
01:10:33.690 --> 01:10:37.030
So he was just happy he got to sit for his background work.
所以他只是很高兴他的背景工作能有椅子坐。

1622
01:10:37.130 --> 01:10:39.510
I'm telling you, I stood for almost nine years.
我跟你说，我站了快九年。

1623
01:10:39.730 --> 01:10:39.970
Yeah.
是啊。

1624
01:10:40.710 --> 01:10:41.650
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

1625
01:10:41.870 --> 01:10:43.310
Well, that was Dream Team.
好了，那是梦幻团队。

1626
01:10:43.670 --> 01:10:45.830
Next up is Michael Scott Paper Company.
接下来是迈克尔·斯科特造纸公司。

1627
01:10:46.030 --> 01:10:49.210
We're going to get busy in that little storage room.
我们要在那个小储藏室里忙活起来了。

1628
01:10:49.370 --> 01:10:50.230
I can't wait.
我等不及了。

1629
01:10:50.410 --> 01:10:50.790
Me too.
我也是。

1630
01:10:51.170 --> 01:10:51.470
All right.
好的。

1631
01:10:51.550 --> 01:10:52.690
Have a great week, you guys.
祝大家有个美好的一周。

1632
01:10:52.850 --> 01:10:53.410
See you then.
到时见。

1633
01:10:59.550 --> 01:11:02.170
Thank you for listening to Office Lady's Second Drink.
感谢收听《办公室女士的第二杯》。

